# The Warmth control under Brightness on the Light page moves the lamp one
# setting a tap, of the eleven it has: plus is warmer, minus is cooler. Each
# end is named and stops there, the settings between are counted from the
# cool end, and the home row says the warmth after the level. Brightness and
# warmth are set apart: a brightness step, to the top of the range included,
# leaves the warmth where it was. A warmth moved while Settings was away is
# read when it comes back, and a refused step is said over both controls.
wait-for Settings
tap-paged Light
wait-for Warmth
expect Brightness
expect 20%
expect 5 of 10
expect Both last until Cobalt closes. The Kobo reader keeps its own brightness and warmth.
expect-missing Lasts until Cobalt closes. The Kobo reader keeps its own level.
expect-missing This version of Cobalt cannot set the warmth on this reader.
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 50
expect-state /device#/warmthSteps 11
expect-state /device#/frontlightPercent 20
shot settings-light-warmth
# Brightness does not move the warmth, at the top of its range or on the
# way back down from it. Before the first brightness step Settings sets the
# warmth to what it already is, so the runtime keeps it.
lifecycle background
device frontlight 95
lifecycle foreground
wait-for 95%
tap-id light-brighter
wait-for 100%
expect 5 of 10
expect-state /device#/frontlightPercent 100
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 50
tap-id light-dimmer
wait-for 95%
expect 5 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 50
lifecycle background
device frontlight 20
lifecycle foreground
wait-for 20%
# One tap is one setting, and the brightness stays where it was.
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 6 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 60
expect-state /device#/frontlightPercent 20
expect 20%
tap-id light-cooler
wait-for 5 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 50
# Up to the warm end, which is named and has nowhere further to go.
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 6 of 10
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 7 of 10
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 8 of 10
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 9 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 90
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for Warmest
expect-missing of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 100
shot settings-light-warmest
# A brightness step leaves the warmth where it was put.
tap-id light-brighter
wait-for 25%
expect Warmest
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 100
expect-state /device#/frontlightPercent 25
tap-id light-dimmer
wait-for 20%
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 100
# A step the runtime refuses leaves the lamp and the reading where they
# were, with the reason over both controls, and the next step that is taken
# clears it.
scenario permission-denied
tap-id light-cooler
wait-for Cobalt did not allow Settings to do that.
expect Warmest
expect 20%
expect-missing Read again
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 100
shot settings-light-warmth-refused
scenario normal
tap-id light-cooler
wait-for 9 of 10
expect-missing Cobalt did not allow Settings to do that.
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 90
# Something else moved the warmth while Settings was in the background, to a
# place between two settings. The lamp takes the nearer one.
lifecycle background
device warmth 12
lifecycle foreground
wait-for 1 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 10
# Down to the cool end, which is named and stops too.
tap-id light-cooler
wait-for Coolest
expect-missing of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 0
shot settings-light-coolest
tap-id light-warmer
wait-for 1 of 10
expect-state /device#/warmthPercent 10
# The home row says the level and then the warmth.
tap-id 4294967295
wait-for Settings
expect Light
expect 20% · Warmth 1 of 10
